                        ],
                        "form": "faddled"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "477a90ac-f671-3e22-86be-439faa346cfa",
                        "entry_id": "e240138e-a29e-32a7-9b1d-4cfada9be0fd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To fiddle (play aimlessly)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d0efaf6-61de-4a52-9c82-8c602b5d54ce",
                                "sense_id": "477a90ac-f671-3e22-86be-439faa346cfa",
                                "text": "I am afraid I must be at bottom, what a cheerful Indian critic has dubbed me, \"a faddling hedonist\" […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56c34386-95c9-469a-acfc-a011090f3f64",
                                "sense_id": "477a90ac-f671-3e22-86be-439faa346cfa",
                                "text": "He faddles over the needless, such as hanging maps up on the walls in the section and putting inkpots on the mantelpiece."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf4c456a-5abe-49e4-8daf-f823c9ee85ff",
                                "sense_id": "477a90ac-f671-3e22-86be-439faa346cfa",
                                "text": "I had that awful woman, Celia Thaxter, sitting next to me, boring me to death with what a marvellous writer Mark Twain was […] I said, \"look, dear, he's sitting just over there. Why don't you go and talk to him?\" She faddled around, blushing like a schoolgirl and saying she couldn't possibly."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8a9b6f0a-6df4-388d-ac3b-f87026f223d7",
                        "entry_id": "e240138e-a29e-32a7-9b1d-4cfada9be0fd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To dote on."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "320264d4-21b7-4b2b-be98-4b81fea21b40",
                                "sense_id": "8a9b6f0a-6df4-388d-ac3b-f87026f223d7",
                                "text": "Even then, when nurse is ready to take baby out for a walk, properly wrapped up, faddling Mamma comes to examine, if not a little corner remains to be closed to the air."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7b429c5-88f1-4c4b-9121-c25e223983a0",
                                "sense_id": "8a9b6f0a-6df4-388d-ac3b-f87026f223d7",
                                "text": "“The last year she spent faddling at Aunt Mai's […] I am not sure this is necessary to her happiness, this faddling after other people. Now, to faddle after folk, who don't want you, is madness . . . but to faddle after those that do is very good employment. Now […] you are the very person for her, for she dotes on you […]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f23a487e-87ec-4600-b909-8cd1b6ca252f",
                                "sense_id": "8a9b6f0a-6df4-388d-ac3b-f87026f223d7",
                                "text": "She was doing no good in church all put about and faddling after Blackie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
